  "slug": "inference-fit-6a61",
  "summary": "Seven preprints dated 12-19 November 2026 present samplers, ML components and pipeline comparisons for LISA, Euclid, LSST DESC and SKA analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is building and validating inference infrastructure for forthcoming cosmological datasets, though the items do not all concern sampler efficiency. ASPIRE reuses existing posteriors for joint cosmological and population inference with dark sirens, reporting 6-28x speedups over reanalysis. samsara++ implements trans-dimensional MCMC in C++/CUDA for LISA global fits with overlapping Galactic binaries and noise. The LSST DESC cluster pipeline is validated on cosmoDC2 mocks, constraining Omega_c and sigma_8. Euclid work addresses ML components: strong-lens detection depends strongly on training-set composition, image format and ensembling, while EuclidFM learns 128-dim embeddings from Q1 photometry. SciPIC-lite provides a public Python library for flexible HOD modelling of clustering observables. SKA SDC3b compares 16 teams' EoR pipelines and finds inter-team variability, which bears on cross-validation of inference methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
